\paragraph{Structural importance.}
For each structure $h$, we compute importance $I(h)$ via first-order Taylor expansion on the reasoning trace loss:
\begin{equation}
    I(h) = \left| \sum_{(x,y) \in \mathcal{D}_\text{cal}} \mathbf{a}_h(x, y)^\top \frac{\partial \mathcal{L}(x, y)}{\partial \mathbf{a}_h} \right|,
    \label{eq:importance}
\end{equation}
where $\mathbf{a}_h$ denotes the activation of structure $h$ and $\mathcal{L}$ is the language modeling loss over the reasoning trace.

tool_args.new_string:
\paragraph{Structural importance.}
For each structure $h$ with activation $\mathbf{a}_h$, we estimate the loss change $\Delta\mathcal{L}$ from removing $h$ (setting $\mathbf{a}_h{=}\mathbf{0}$).
First-order Taylor expansion gives $\Delta\mathcal{L} = \mathcal{L}(\mathbf{a}_h{=}\mathbf{0}) - \mathcal{L}(\mathbf{a}_h) \approx -\mathbf{a}_h^\top \nabla_{\mathbf{a}_h}\mathcal{L}$, dropping $O(\|\mathbf{a}_h\|^2)$ terms.
Aggregating over the calibration set and taking the absolute value:
\begin{equation}
    I(h) = \left| \sum_{(x,y) \in \mathcal{D}_\text{cal}} \mathbf{a}_h(x, y)^\top \frac{\partial \mathcal{L}(x, y)}{\partial \mathbf{a}_h} \right|,
    \label{eq:importance}
\end{equation}
where $\mathcal{L}$ is the language modeling loss over the reasoning trace.

